--- /dev/null
+++ b/rust/corpus/sim-exempt.tsv
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+# Reds of the seeded gate ruled not to be defects, read by
+# crates/rexx-exec/tests/concurrency_tests.rs, sim_gate. Tab-separated columns: group, part,
+# test, kind, a text the red's line holds (its refusal where it has one), each * for any; then the
+# reason and its evidence. A kind is panic, crash, hang, invariant, determinism, design-limit,
+# check or no-report. Each row is as narrow as its evidence (controller rulings, Task 10).
+base/class/MutexSemaphore.testGroup	single	TEST_EXCLUSION	design-limit	a wait in the simulation mode that only a signal can end	the test's own race (ruling P46): main takes the mutex between the worker's step = 6 and its last acquire and never releases it, so the worker waits forever; the oracle reaches the same deadlock in that interleaving	the oracle hangs 3 of 3 at rc 137 on docs/superpowers/records/2026-10-01-phase-6-s2-s5/exclusion-every-hang.rex; under uniform:1 the whole part ends in this refusal on 60 of 60 seeds and passes 60 of 60 with TEST_EXCLUSION left out (Task 10 report, R4)
+base/rexxutil/SysSleep.testGroup	*	TEST_SLEEP_DURATION	check	*	the test asserts host sleep latency: its lower bound needs at least 1 us measured after SysSleep(1e-8), which a real system gets only from nanosleep's overshoot, and the spec models no sleep latency (controller ruling, Task 10 carry)	under sim the virtual clock jumps to the 10 ns deadline and time('E') reads 0 (task-9-report.md, Concern 2); nanosleep overshoots 51 to 110 us on this host (review of Task 9, check 6)
+corpus/lang/message_notify.rex	program	-	design-limit	a wait that nothing left to run can end	the program's own race: a ~notify landing while the notified message's activity runs its notification loop is never sent messageComplete, in the oracle (MessageClass.cpp:217-229, :666-685) as here (notify_parties), so the later ~wait never ends	docs/superpowers/records/2026-10-07-phase-6-1/notify-window.md: the oracle hangs 5 of 5 on notify-window.rex, which forces that interleaving (Task 10 report, R5)
